{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For any man, any man who curses his father.</b> It refers to what is written above: 'and you shall keep all my statutes' etc. That is, it is fitting that you fulfill my commandments, for if a man curses his father and his mother etc. And since there is punishment for one who disgraces his father and mother, all the more so I have cause upon you to keep my commandments, for I am your father, your king, and your creator." "<b>His father.</b> And not his father's father. And his mother — and not his mother's mother." "<b>His father and his mother he cursed.</b> Scripture attached 'cursed' to his father and attached 'cursed' to his mother, to make him liable for this one without that one." "<b>His father and his mother he cursed.</b> The verse repeated it on account of its blood being in him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:46.026351064Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}